CORRECTED_SIGNATURE_SCAN_LOGIC
1. Read the frozen Checks source as numbered lines.
2. Select every line matching ^[[:space:]]*#check[[:space:]]+([A-Za-z0-9_'.]+)[[:space:]]*$.
3. Require exactly the 27 resulting directives on source lines 11 through 37;
   the source itself, not a hard-coded minimum, determines the expected count.
4. For each pair (sourceLine, checkName), find exactly one direct-checks-r9.log
   record whose first line matches:
   ^info: lean/PvNP/RealizableHardness/ActualMZ24FixedRhoPointwiseSelectorChecks[.]lean:<sourceLine>:0: (?<decl>[^ ]+)
5. Remove an optional Lean universe suffix .{...} from decl, take the terminal
   component after the final period, and require it to equal checkName exactly.
6. Fail on a missing record, duplicate record, name mismatch, unexpected source
   #check directive, or unexpected target signature record.

The original wrapper instead expected PvNP at column 1 of the log and required
at least 28 matches. Lean 4.34 emitted the signatures after an info/source-location
prefix, and the frozen source contains exactly 27 #check directives. Therefore
the original extraction count 0 and minimum 28 were wrapper assumptions, not
missing signatures.

